[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 1"""
 date="2026-02-18T15:35:41Z"
 content="""
I have the file here but git log says it's only changed once since it
appeared in August. Checking another machine, the file is unchanged since
2024.

It seems the file will only change if /usr's mtime is changed. It's fairly
rare for a new top-level item to be added/removed to /usr, which is what
changes the mtime of the directory.

This file is not configuration per se, but if the system is set up to do
offline updates, it seems to me that you would want to preserve it? Also,
since the offline updates do modify /etc, the change to the file that gets
committed at the same time would document that offline update caused it,
which seems desirable.
"""]]
